e holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. |\n73: | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n74: | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), or a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`). |\n75: | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: ## 5. CONFIGURATION\n80: \n81: | Setting | Default | Purpose |\n82: |---|---|---|\n83: | sk-code surface | OPENCODE | Applies OpenCode TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Shell and config conventions. |\n84: | README scope | Direct folder | This file documents this folder, not sibling folders. |\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 6. USAGE EXAMPLES\n89: \n90: **Audit this folder**\n91: \n92: ```text\n93: User request: Check .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy for sk-code and README coverage.\n94: Skill routing: sk-code plus sk-doc.\n95: Expected